tion, beats everything.\n        13. Quadplex set: a quad with two single cards OR two pairs attached.\n        Use the EXACT card symbols provided in the Valid Moves list.\n        Prepare a valid JSON object like {"cards": ["♠3", "♥3"]} for your answer, along with your explanation and reason. If you pass, output: {"cards": []}\n        \n        Now is your turn, to your best ability, choose your move to maximize your chances of winning.\n        Please briefly evaluate a few proimsing moves, provide reason for your final choice, and output the action with specified format.\n        Your response format should be:\n        Evaluation: [Your Evaluation]\n        Reason: [Your Reason]\n        Answer: [Your Answer]\n    ', 'user_prompt': "You are playing as the landlord. The landlord's aim is to be the first to play out all his cards in valid combinations. If any of the other players manages to play all their cards before the landlord, you lose.\nYou are the Landlord. Both the Next Player (Right) and the Previous Player (Left) are Peasants and are your ENEMIES. You fight alone. The objective is to empty your hand as fast as possible.\n\nYour Hand: ♥4 ♦4 ♦5 ♠9 ♥9 ♦9 ♦2\nLast Play to Beat: ♠Q\n--- Game History (Recent) ---\nTurn 9 (You): Pass\nTurn 10 (Next Player): Pass\nTurn 10 (Prev Player): ♠4 ♣4\nTurn 10 (You): ♠6 ♣6\nTurn 11 (Next Player): ♥Q ♦Q\nTurn 11 (Prev Player): ♥2 ♣2\nTurn 11 (You): Pass\nTurn 12 (Next Player): Pass\nTurn 12 (Prev Player): ♥5 ♣5\nTurn 12 (You): ♣8 ♦8\nTurn 13 (Next Player): Pass\nTurn 13 (Prev Player): ♥A ♣A\nTurn 13 (You): Pass\nTurn 14 (Next Player): Pass\nTurn 14 (Prev Player): ♠Q\n--- Player Info ---\nCards Held by Next Player (Right) [Peasant (Opponent)]: 4\nCards Held by Prev Player (Left) [Peasant (Opponent)]: 4\n--- Cards Remaining Unknown (Card Counting) ---\n(Format explanation: 'Rank: Count', e.g., '2: 4' means there are four 2s left unknown)\nBlackJoker: 1, K: 2, 10: 4, 3: 1\nValid Moves:\nsingle: ♦2\npass: []\n\nSelect the best move from the Valid Moves list above. You can choose to pass even if you have valid moves that can beat the previous play, but you cannot pass if you are in a Free Play (no last play).\nEnsure your response matches one of the valid moves exactly.\nRemember to provide Explanation, Reason, and Answer.", 'reasoning': "**Okay, here's the plan, and it's a bold one.**  I'm going to lead with the 2 of Diamonds, `♦2`. It's the highest card I've got and it *must* win this trick. I have a Full House (9, 9, 9, 4, 4) in my hand, and both my opponents are out of the cards needed to fight back.\n\nI need this round to play out as a forced win. My hand is a triplet of 9s, a pair of 4s, and a single 5, so with this two leading I can execute my 'kill combo' as it were.\n\nThe situation looks good. The player on my left only has three cards remaining, the player on my right has four, which means neither can beat my 3-with-2 in terms of size or type. With this lead, I'll play out a full house. I'll get to play my Full House. They can't beat that with a normal play.\n\nMy 2 is only threatened by a Joker or a bomb of some sort. There are four 10s missing, so it's *possible* they have a bomb, but with this hand it's an okay play.  I'm basically holding the equivalent of a winning lottery ticket if the bomb is not out there.\n\nThen, they'll be left with nothing. I know there are risks, of course. Maybe the Joker is in play. But, with a strong structured hand like this, going for the win now is my highest-percentage play. The 2 is my only way to secure the win. It is the decisive opening that will lock in this game. So, my play is `♦2`.\n\n\n", 'output': 'Evaluation: The current situation is critical. The Previous Player played a ♠Q, and they have only 3 cards left. The Next Player has 4 cards left. My hand is {4, 4, 5, 9, 9, 9, 2}.\nI have a very strong path to victory if I can take control. My hand consists of a Single 2, a Single 5, and a Full House (99944).\nCrucially, a Full House requires 5 cards. Since both opponents have 4 or fewer cards, **neither of them can play a Full House**. This means my Full House (99944) is unbeatable by any normal combination; only a Bomb can stop it.\nThere are four 10s unaccounted for, so a Bomb is possible. However, I cannot play around a Bomb passively. The best strategy is to force the game.\nIf I play the ♦2 and win the trick:\n1. I play the Full House 99944.\n2. Opponents cannot beat it (insufficient cards).\n3. I am left with a single 5. If my Full House clears, I play the 5. If the 5 is beaten, I still have a chance if they lead a small card, but often I might win outright if they passed on the 2. (Actually, if I play 2 -> Win -> 99944 -> Win -> 5, I win the game, unless they bomb).\n\nIf I pass:\nI risk losing control. Left might lead a card I cannot beat efficiently, or Right might enter and change the flow. I must use the 2 to secure the line for my Full House.\n\nReason: The ♦2 is the highest card I hold and beats the current ♠Q. Winning this trick allows me to play the Full House 99944. Since both opponents hold fewer than 5 cards, they cannot play a Full House to beat mine. This makes the sequence [2 -> 99944 -> 5] a forced win path unless an opponent holds a Bomb (Four 10s). Passing gives up this guaranteed non-bomb advantage.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♦2"]}'}
